## 1. Project Overview

### 1.1 Game Description

**Dogfight2** is a turn-based WEGO (We-Go) aerial combat simulation game set in World War 2 (and World War 1). The game features a unique turn-based system where players plan maneuvers during an "Order Phase" and then watch all aircraft execute simultaneously during an "Execution Phase."

**Genre:** Turn-Based Tactical Combat / Flight Simulation  
**Era:** WW1 and WW2  
**Perspective:** Top-down view with altitude scaling  
**Gameplay Style:** Tactical planning with simultaneous execution

### 1.2 Technology Stack

- **Language:** JavaScript (ES6+)
- **Platform:** Web Browser (HTML5)
- **Rendering:** HTML5 Canvas 2D API
- **Audio:** Web Audio API
- **Architecture:** Single-page application (monolithic HTML file)
- **Dependencies:** Minimal (Playwright for testing only)

### 1.3 Project Status

**Completion:** 81% (13 out of 16 planned enhancements implemented)

**Status:** Fully playable with comprehensive features including:
- 9+ aircraft types (WW2) + 18 WW1 aircraft
- 10 campaign missions
- Component-based damage system
- Weather system
- Formation/wingman mechanics
- Hot-seat multiplayer
- Replay system
- Ground attack capabilities

